WEBVTT

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.940
Kaito... Run for it!

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.240
Don’t get mixed up... 
with the Puzzle of Fools!

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:21.250
Run, Kaito...!

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.730
Jin, are you okay? Jin!

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.020
What was I...?

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:29.940
You mentioned someone 
named, “Kaito.”

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.500
It was a dream...

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.630
Who is Kaito?

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.320
He’s a... friend.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.890
A very special one.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:57.010
Kaito is his dear friend?

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:13.190
What do you want at this early hour?

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:16.630
Good morning! Isn’t 
this weather lovely?

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.450
Why don’t you hurry 
and state your business?

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.080
I’d like to invite you to dinner.

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:27.520
The main dish is...

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:29.630
Kaito Daimon.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:09.000
A Good Meal can 
Resolve Most Problems

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:16.590
Ya-hoo!

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:20.090
Ya-hoo with a ya-hoo!

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:23.590
Ya-hoo with a ya-hoo!

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:25.970
Give it a try, Kaito! Jin!

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:29.200
We came on this picnic 
to kick back and relax,

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:32.830
so why don’t you holler, 
“Ya-hoo,” with me?

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:36.590
We’re on the mountain 
behind campus.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:42.720
Kaito, don’t be such 
a stick in the mud!

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.110
Let’s hear a “Ya-hoo!”

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:45.640
That hurt!

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:47.080
Something kinda...

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:49.180
smells burnt.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:53.580
Oh, crap!

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:55.560
It’s smoking!

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:59.090
Nonoha is always full 
of life, isn’t she?

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:01.360
Our most expensive 
meat is getting burnt!

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:02.570
She has energy to burn.

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:06.280
Kaito, you two are very close since you’ve
known each other since you were little.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:10.410
I’m jealous of how you have
your childhood memories.

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:14.100
You still can’t remember anything?

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:20.300
Sorry, my bad. I don’t 
mean to be pushy.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:24.130
I know. I think it would be nice if
I could remember my past.

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:27.350
Such as when I was 
with you and Rook.

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:30.640
As well as when I lived 
together with Raetsel.

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:34.520
But if I regain the 
memories I’ve lost,

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:39.500
I might end up hurting 
either you or Raetsel.

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:42.360
I do not want to hurt anyone.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:44.280
I do not want anyone to get hurt.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:48.570
Must I remember,
knowing what the cost could be?

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:54.710
Jin, even so, I want you 
to remember everything.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:58.520
The Jin I knew was always
smiling in front of puzzles.

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:05.030
That time was precious to me and
I think it was to you as well.

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:12.660
So I want you to remember what you--what
we--viewed as precious time together.

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:15.320
Thank you, Kaito.

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:18.350
I am truly happy to 
hear you say that.

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:19.560
But Raetsel...

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:21.050
I feel the same.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:24.210
Raetsel!

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:32.120
Jin, I want you to remember.

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:38.160
Remember the precious 
time you spent with me.

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:38.850
And then...

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:42.860
remember how much you hated puzzles.

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:46.070
You’re wrong there!

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:52.510
Poor Kaito, but I’ll forgive you.

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:57.580
After all, you simply 
don’t know any better.

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:14.100
The torment a Puzzle of 
Fools put Jin through...

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:16.320
You don’t know about that.

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:19.960
After all, that happened 
after he left you.

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:25.530
This is the real Jin, 
who only I know.

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:33.740
Jin!

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:38.750
Why...? Why does such 
a cruel puzzle exist?

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:41.100
Why, Raetsel?!

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:43.000
Why?!

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:46.880
You don’t have to 
say anything, Jin...

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:49.740
You’re okay. You’re okay now...

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:57.500
Jin, remember!

00:06:57.910 --> 00:06:59.270
Remember the real you.

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:04.270
I... don’t know. I...!

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:05.900
Stop it!

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:08.400
Don’t hurt Jin!

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:12.070
The one hurting Jin, Kaito, is you.

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:17.560
Right now, you’re 
a Puzzle of Fools!

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:20.430
The type that will do nothing
but hurt and agonize Jin.

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:23.640
Jin, it’ll be okay.

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:24.840
You have me.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:30.030
I’m about to blow a fuse!

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:33.540
Kaito went on a picnic with Jin?!

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:35.840
And they dragged Nonoha 
along with them?!

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:37.720
What if something happens?!

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:42.750
Are you worried that Raetsel or one of the
Master Brains might go after them again?

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:46.250
But Rae-Rae may not 
be such a bad kid.

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:48.300
Don’t be such a softy!

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:52.110
Your “Rae-Rae” has President Enigma
wrapped around her finger.

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:54.930
It wouldn’t hurt to keep 
our guard up around her.

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:58.150
There is something about 
her I just don’t like.

00:07:58.150 --> 00:08:03.140
I can’t stand how she’s using
puzzles to muddle Kaito’s heart.

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:07.630
I, Ana, think that 
Rae-Rae is like Kaito.

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:13.040
Hey, you don’t think she’s
wearing an Armlet, do you?

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:16.370
I had Iwashimizu conduct a search,
but she’s clean.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:16.910
Clean.

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:19.930
Raetsel is using her own mind
to make these puzzles.

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:23.050
She truly is like Kaito.

00:08:23.050 --> 00:08:26.540
At any rate, I don’t 
like Raetsel or Enigma!

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:41.030
Now then, how should I go
about helping Kaito...?

00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:44.440
Suspicious character approaching.
Suspicious character approaching.

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:52.130
That was dangerous!

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:56.030
I was about to say 
the same to you, boy.

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:04.760
A robot?

00:09:04.760 --> 00:09:07.270
You’re riding a rather 
fascinating toy, boy.

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:11.150
Alas, I am afraid it fails 
to elicit any ecstasy.

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:14.260
Don’t make fun of Iwashimizu!

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:16.410
Don’t make fun of Iwashimizu!

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:19.600
That’s the Republic 
of Amgine’s...!

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:22.850
Oh, for you to recognize 
the coat of arms...

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:29.420
You have a bounty, but 
it is a measly $650,000.

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:31.820
Even a baby could look 
at the math and tell

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:36.570
that defeating Kaito Daimon would
fill me with far more ecstasy!

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:38.740
You could never defeat Kaito!

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:45.000
I cannot let that slide.

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:51.610
No one stands a chance before the
great mathemagician, Dr. Theorem!

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:54.050
You’re a mathemagician?

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:58.610
When it comes to numbers,
even Kaito can’t beat me.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:02.490
Before you boast, try solving this!

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:03.620
Try!

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:14.880
That is beautiful! However...

00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:16.380
The answer is...

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:24.580
123 - 45 - 67 + 89 = 100!

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:27.640
It’s far too easy.

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:30.070
It looks like you’re pretty good,

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:33.900
but your ability to solve that simple puzzle
doesn’t make you a mathemagician!

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:36.090
Fight me...

00:10:36.670 --> 00:10:37.900
before you face Kaito!

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:40.890
You are being rather silly, boy.

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:41.780
But I am game.

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:46.340
My fight with you shall 
serve as a warm-up.

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:49.600
Come to the puzzle 
stage I have set up!

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:16.690
Don’t make fun of Iwashimizu.

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:19.220
Don’t make fun of Iwashimizu.

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:21.130
You built a puzzle up here?

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:33.060
Now, find the most 
beautiful numeric value,

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:36.280
which is hidden within this
list of dazzling numbers!

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:41.780
If you love numbers, it should be
easy for you to solve, boy!

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:47.580
The most beautiful numeric value?

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:48.580
All right!

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:57.190
First I’ve got to find the pattern
in the line of numbers!

00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:04.530
No!

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:07.100
That isn’t it, either.

00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:10.040
What’s going on?

00:12:10.470 --> 00:12:12.170
Having difficulty, boy?

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:13.730
You were all talk.

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:15.250
Your irrational logic is 
falling flat, isn’t it?

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:16.940
I’m just getting started!

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:20.480
No, wrong again...

00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:22.650
Same for this one...!

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:28.010
Ah, such beauty! It is the height
of numerical ecstasy!

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:31.500
I imagine you are still 
too young to understand.

00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:34.040
It makes me tremble with delight!

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:37.500
What?!

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:39.130
This slipped my mind.

00:12:39.130 --> 00:12:42.300
If you fail to solve the 
puzzle within the time limit,

00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:45.910
your life will be burnt asunder
by the flames of ecstasy!

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:47.650
N-no!

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:51.910
Our goal is the annihilation 
of all puzzlers.

00:12:52.430 --> 00:12:55.920
The Phi-Brain children
must serve as an example!

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:03.420
At least I shall let you die in
a blaze of ecstasy, boy!

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:13.430
Kaito, I’ll tell you one other thing
about the Jin you don’t know.

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:15.040
What?

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:18.090
“Puzzles are chains. 
Puzzles are mirrors.”

00:13:18.090 --> 00:13:19.560
Those were your words.

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:21.090
My...?

00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:24.050
Puzzles bind people like chains.

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:26.820
Like mirrors, they reflect aspects of
ourselves that we don’t want to see.

00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:30.720
Isn’t that why you hated 
puzzles, Jin? Right?

00:13:31.390 --> 00:13:34.450
They bind people and reflect
what we don’t want to see...

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:36.830
Right. Please remember, Jin.

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:40.590
Remember what you taught
me all those years ago!

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:47.030
What’s wrong, bird friend?

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:51.810
Eh?! Q-taro is what?!

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:54.090
Gammon!

00:13:54.090 --> 00:13:55.310
What?

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:58.980
You’re lying! Jin 
would never say that!

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:01.340
Jin...

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:05.240
When I was starting to hate puzzles,

00:14:05.800 --> 00:14:07.840
Jin taught me to see 
them in a new light.

00:14:09.590 --> 00:14:11.890
He taught me how much 
fun puzzles could be!

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:18.550
So I’m going to believe 
in the Jin whom I know!

00:14:18.550 --> 00:14:21.710
The Jin I knew never hated puzzles!

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:25.970
No! The Jin I knew 
was the one true Jin!

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:27.970
Your Jin was just some fraud!

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:33.780
Stop right there!

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:35.350
Nonoha?

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:40.930
We’re supposed to be on a picnic,
so wipe off that scary scowl!

00:14:40.930 --> 00:14:43.040
I managed to grill up a mean BBQ!

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:43.980
Now eat up!

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:46.920
Look, now isn’t the time.

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:49.550
He’s right! Don’t butt 
into our conversation.

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:51.740
Take a time out! Enjoy 
a nice, quiet meal.

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:56.210
Humans never think straight
on an empty stomach.

00:14:56.210 --> 00:15:00.650
Most problems can be resolved
once you’ve eaten a good meal.

00:15:00.650 --> 00:15:02.310
Here! Jin, have some.

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:03.940
Go on!

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:09.120
Jin!

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:10.050
Are you all right?

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:12.280
You shouldn’t have 
eaten that onion!

00:15:12.280 --> 00:15:15.030
No kidding! You 
can’t stand onions.

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:15.030
Jin, are you all right?

00:15:15.030 --> 00:15:16.310
Hang in there! Jin!

00:15:15.030 --> 00:15:16.310
Drink some water! Water!

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:18.870
This isn’t funny, Nonoha!

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:26.190
You two were just arguing over which
one of you remembered the real Jin,

00:15:26.600 --> 00:15:28.590
but don’t some of 
your memories match up?

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:35.390
I don’t know Jin all that well and
I don’t know what the real Jin was like,

00:15:35.390 --> 00:15:38.770
but both of you are genuinely
concerned about Jin.

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:42.940
I can tell that your 
feelings for him are real.

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:44.710
Isn’t that enough?

00:15:45.980 --> 00:15:47.460
Nonoha...

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:53.160
That’s...

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:54.470
Isn’t this...?

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:01.850
That must be it!

00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:11.130
Q-taro!

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:12.790
This looks bad!

00:16:12.790 --> 00:16:14.280
Oh, isn’t that...?

00:16:18.850 --> 00:16:22.540
If you love numbers,
it should be easy for you to solve!

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:24.790
Cubik!

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:26.860
Kaito?

00:16:29.610 --> 00:16:30.630
What’s with these numbers?

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:33.380
Is it a puzzle?

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:53.320
Jin...

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:56.500
Cubik, what’s the hold up?

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:57.970
Isn’t this your specialty?

00:16:57.970 --> 00:16:59.080
I don’t know!

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:02.480
I’ve tried every possibility 
I could think of.

00:17:03.020 --> 00:17:05.080
So the main performer 
has taken the stage?

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:07.980
I am most lenient, you see.

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:10.440
I shall allow you to work
together to solve this puzzle.

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:12.960
It shall further 
heighten the ecstasy!

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:21.200
It’s gotten bigger?!

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:23.960
How beautiful!

00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:26.850
Can you solve it? Or is 
that irrational thinking?

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:30.190
It’s beyond you! Clearly, 
you can’t solve it!

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:32.050
Damn it!

00:17:32.050 --> 00:17:35.110
The lineup is completely different!

00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:37.300
The answer is still the same.

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:39.550
It is the most beautiful number!

00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:43.650
The answer is the same
regardless the panel’s size?

00:17:43.650 --> 00:17:49.810
But what type of number could
have 18 digits or 36 digits?

00:17:51.650 --> 00:17:53.650
An infinite number...?

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:57.130
This might be an irrational number!

00:17:57.660 --> 00:17:58.910
An irrational number?

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:04.080
If we put a decimal point here,
it would become 1.4142...

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:08.120
1.41421356... 
It’s the square root of two.

00:18:08.710 --> 00:18:10.710
The square root of two,
which is an irrational number,

00:18:10.710 --> 00:18:12.920
was hidden diagonally 
across the square!

00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:17.650
So that’s why he used the
word “irrational” earlier!

00:18:18.550 --> 00:18:21.700
I’ve figured it out! 
The answer is--

00:18:22.140 --> 00:18:23.310
Wait!

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:25.700
He also said...

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:27.890
The answer is still the same.

00:18:27.890 --> 00:18:29.870
It is the most beautiful number!

00:18:30.900 --> 00:18:32.150
In which case...!

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:36.010
Found it!

00:18:36.570 --> 00:18:38.170
It’s pi!

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:42.690
I see! It’s the most 
beautiful number!

00:18:42.690 --> 00:18:43.930
Yeah, it sure is!

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:47.740
The numeric code is pi!

00:18:47.740 --> 00:18:49.940
He’s looking for the golden ratio.

00:18:51.750 --> 00:19:00.820
In other words, the answer is
1.618033988749894848204586834365

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:07.600
63811772030917980576!

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:11.650
The golden ratio! 
What a beautiful sound!

00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:14.770
There’s no puzzle I--no, we--

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:16.360
Kaito!

00:19:19.490 --> 00:19:23.140
There’s no puzzle 
we can’t solve!

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:33.730
Retreat! Retreat!

00:19:39.010 --> 00:19:42.740
Ecstasy!

00:20:01.280 --> 00:20:02.010
Kaito!

00:20:02.910 --> 00:20:04.510
Q-taro!

00:20:04.910 --> 00:20:06.200
Iwami, are you okay?

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:08.010
Yeah, I am fine.

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:08.010
Sorry to have made you worry.

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:08.910
Really!

00:20:10.830 --> 00:20:12.000
Are you all right?

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:13.630
Uh-huh, but...

00:20:13.630 --> 00:20:14.400
What’s wrong?

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:17.640
I wanted to protect you, Kaito.

00:20:17.640 --> 00:20:22.780
But in the end, I needed you to save me even
though number puzzles are my forte.

00:20:25.470 --> 00:20:27.150
That’s not true.

00:20:27.150 --> 00:20:29.760
That puzzle woulda been too
much for me on my own.

00:20:29.760 --> 00:20:32.040
I would have lost without you.

00:20:32.730 --> 00:20:34.770
Thank you, Cubik.

00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:37.610
Really? I guess you’re right!

00:20:37.610 --> 00:20:39.780
You’d be nowhere without me.

00:20:40.190 --> 00:20:41.050
Whoa, there!

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:47.410
Jin!

00:20:47.410 --> 00:20:48.660
Stay back!

00:20:51.870 --> 00:20:54.810
I was wrong to leave Jin with you.

00:20:57.380 --> 00:20:59.050
I’m sorry, Jin.

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:02.940
I was supposed to be 
there to protect you...

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:06.340
Jin, it’ll be okay. 
You’ve got me.

00:21:06.890 --> 00:21:09.390
My Jin... You’re all mine...

00:21:28.490 --> 00:21:30.850
Here! It should be ready.

00:21:31.540 --> 00:21:35.040
But you failed to cook Kaito.

00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:39.090
Despite that fact, you seem to
be in a rather good mood.

00:21:39.500 --> 00:21:41.860
Did something nice happen?

00:21:42.760 --> 00:21:44.990
I’ve told you that I hate onions!

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:48.550
You want to mimic 
the person you love.

00:21:49.100 --> 00:21:51.060
You can be cute when 
you choose to be.

00:21:51.470 --> 00:21:52.620
Ow!

00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:57.960
That’s what you get for saying
things you shouldn’t.

00:21:59.810 --> 00:22:01.960
Actually, I wouldn’t be so sure.

00:22:18.250 --> 00:22:21.610
Is there truly a side to 
Jin that I don’t know?

00:22:22.130 --> 00:22:23.980
Is that true, Jin?

00:24:04.630 --> 00:24:08.710
I wonder if Kaito, Rook and
Raetsel can get along...

00:24:09.030 --> 00:24:11.300
Please allow me to 
work with Master Rook.

00:24:11.300 --> 00:24:12.300
Mr. Bishop?!

00:24:12.300 --> 00:24:15.430
Harmonious communication begins
from moderate laughter.

00:24:15.430 --> 00:24:16.430
Let’s put these on him.

00:24:16.430 --> 00:24:17.430
Aren’t those cat ears?

00:24:17.430 --> 00:24:19.640
Next time, “I Get that Feeling.”

00:24:18.510 --> 00:24:28.000
I Get that Feeling

00:24:20.200 --> 00:24:22.020
These should neuter 
all of our pawblems.

00:24:22.020 --> 00:24:23.020
Cat’s caught my tongue!

00:24:28.000 --> 00:24:30.970
Fin
Art: Akeru Otsuki
